I recall that the overall design guidelines for Glint emphasize that the model should never claim success while any required action failed. Instead, the system should surface a warning so the model can read the error messages, fix the underlying cause, and retry. The best place to inject such a warning is right where the tool results are formatted, because that string is what gets sent back to the model as part of the response. If I append a warning when there are any `status: "error"` entries, the model will see it in its next turn and can react accordingly.

